          "text": "An architectural exploration of message anatomy: classifying Command, Event, and Document intents, engineering non-blocking asynchronous request-reply, and enforcing correlation semantics.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-callout-note",
      "_type": "callout",
      "tone": "note",
      "title": "EIP Part 3 \u2014 Upcoming Series Installment",
      "items": [
        {
          "_key": "note-item-2",
          "title": "This architectural deep dive is currently in active development as part of the 8-part Enterprise Integration Patterns series on wiki.eiakoji.me. The formal theoretical derivations, Excalidraw-style schematics, Little's Law/queueing equations, and production Java 21 reference implementations will land directly in this publication entry.",
          "status": "upcoming"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-h2-patterns",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-h2-patterns-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "2. Pattern Catalog & Formal Realizations",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-p-patterns-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-p-patterns-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "In this installment, we formalize the following core integration patterns established by Gregor Hohpe and Bobby Woolf, mapping each to its modern cloud-native realization:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Command Message: Intent-driven message instructing a specific downstream recipient to perform a transactional action (e.g. CQRS command payload).",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Document Message: State-carrying message transferring an explicit snapshot of domain state without prescriptive execution orders.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Event Message: Immutable notification that a discrete domain state transition has occurred (e.g. OrderPlaced, PaymentAuthorized).",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-03",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-03-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Request-Reply: Two-way conversational messaging over asynchronous channels, linking requests to replies without holding open TCP connections.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-04",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-04-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Return Address: Header metadata specifying the reply destination channel to which response messages must be delivered.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-05",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-05-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Correlation Identifier: Unique request token header (e.g. W3C traceparent or correlationId) enabling callers to match inbound responses with inflight requests.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-06",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-06-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Message Sequence: Ordering metadata (sequence IDs, total chunk counts, partition offsets) enabling reassembly of fragmented streams.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-07",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-07-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Message Expiration: Time-to-live (TTL) headers enabling brokers and consumers to discard stale messages that are no longer operationally valid.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-pat-08",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-pat-08-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Format Indicator: Envelope metadata specifying the serialization format or schema registry version identifier (e.g. CloudEvents datacontenttype).",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-h2-invariants",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-h2-invariants-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "3. Invariants, Failure Modes & Physical Constraints",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-p-invariants-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-p-invariants-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Engineering resilient enterprise integration topologies requires analyzing the exact failure boundaries and physical constraints governing these patterns:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-inv-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-inv-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Intent Classification: Blurring Command and Event semantics creates tight distributed coupling; Events announce facts to autonomous subscribers, while Commands enforce execution expectations on specific processors.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-inv-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-inv-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Asynchronous Correlation Leaks: Temporary reply queues and in-memory correlation maps leak resources if upstream clients crash before responses return; robust systems enforce strict expiration windows.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-02-inv-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-02-inv-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Clock Skew in Expiration: Message expiration based on absolute wall-clock timestamps fails under distributed clock drift; relative TTL offsets provide resilience against unsynchronized node clocks.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    }
  ]
}